1,Maklew Language (MGF) – L1 & L2 Speakers... | Ethnologue Free,https://www.ethnologue.com/language/mgf/,"Maklew is an endangered indigenous language of Indonesia. It belongs to the South-Central Papuan language family. The language is used as a first language by all adults in the ethnic community, but not all young people.",Maklew,South-Central Papuan
2,Maklew - mgf (South-Central Papuan) - PeopleGroups.org,https://peoplegroups.org/language/mgf/,"Maklew (mgf) is part of the South-Central Papuan family and South-Central Papuan, Yelmek-Maklew class.No entries found for the specified language code: Maklew (mgf).",Maklew,South-Central Papuan
3,Maklew language — Grokipedia,https://grokipedia.com/page/maklew_language,"Maklew (ISO 639-3: mgf; also spelled Makleu or Makaleo), closely related to Yelmek, is an endangered Papuan language spoken by approximately 100–200 people (as of the 2020s) in Welbuti village, Merauke Regency, South Papua province, Indonesia.",Maklew,South-Central Papuan
4,Maklew,https://docs.verbix.com/EndangeredLanguages/Maklew,"Language family: South-Central Papuan, Yelmek-Maklew (SIL classification). Number of speakers: 120. Vulnerability: Endangered.",Maklew,South-Central Papuan
5,"Full text of ""enwiki-Maklew_language-20200726.pdf""",https://archive.org/stream/enwiki-Maklew_language-20200726.pdf/enwiki-Maklew_language-20200726_djvu.txt,"Live Music Archive Librivox Free Audio.Maklew (Makleu) is a language of the proposed Trans-Fly - Bulaka River family in West Papua. It is spoken in Welbuti village, Merauke Regency. References. 1. Maklew at Ethnologue (8th ed., 1974). Note: Data may come from an earlier edition.",Maklew,South-Central Papuan
6,A Documentation and Description of Yelmek and Maklew,https://openresearch-repository.anu.edu.au/server/api/core/bitstreams/c3745b16-1b53-459a-b769-e314828e2663/content,(2017) the evidence for a South-Central Papuan family containing these three groups is too weak. They consider it safer to treat Yelmek-Maklew as an independent family. Proof or disproof of this classification can only be found when more extensive data is available.,Maklew,South-Central Papuan
7,Maklew language - Wikiwand,https://www.wikiwand.com/en/Maklew_language,"Maklew is a language of the proposed Trans-Fly – Bulaka River family in South Papua, Indonesia. It is known to be spoken in Welbuti village, Merauke Regency.",Maklew,South-Central Papuan
